# LeadDesk Mini — Django REST Framework API (Backend)

Built for the **Digital Heroes Internship Qualification Task (Role 04: Full Stack Development)**.

- **GitHub Repository**: https://github.com/swagath088/digital-heroes
- **Base API URL**: https://leaddesk-backend-63q9.onrender.com/api/
- **Health Check Endpoint**: https://leaddesk-backend-63q9.onrender.com/health/
- **Frontend App**: https://digitalheroesfntend.vercel.app/

---

## 🛠️ Architecture & Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Django 4.2 & Django REST Framework
- **Language**: Python 3.11
- **Database**: SQLite / Django ORM
- **Authentication**: Custom REST view validating Django Superusers via `django.contrib.auth.authenticate()`
- **CORS Configuration**: Configured via `django-cors-headers` to accept requests from Vercel origins.

---

## 📋 API Contract

### 1. Submit & List Leads
- **Endpoint**: `POST /api/leads/` | `GET /api/leads/`
- **Search Filter**: `GET /api/leads/?search=term` (Filters by `full_name` or `email`)

### 2. Update Lead Status
- **Endpoint**: `PATCH /api/leads/<id>/`
- **Payload**: `{"status": "Contacted"}`

### 3. Admin Authentication
- **Endpoint**: `POST /api/auth/login/`
- **Payload**: `{"email": "sswagath46@gmail.com", "password": "yourpassword"}`

---

## 🤖 AI Usage Disclosure
AI tools (ChatGPT/Gemini) were utilized during backend development to assist with error rectification (such as resolving `ALLOWED_HOSTS` and CORS configurations), implementing the `/health/` check endpoint for Render uptime monitoring, and setting up initial Django REST Framework view structures. All logic was manually verified, tested, and adjusted to ensure seamless data persistence and authentication.
